Dev tools for the desk's avatar. Not shipped; harness doesn't use them.

  fetch-desk-assets.sh DIR
      MediaPipe's fit files into DIR/mediapipe/, checked by SHA-256.
      DIR is what the desk serves as /desk/assets/ (the data folder's
      desk-assets/).

  devserver.py PORT DATA [--csp POLICY | --no-csp] [--cache]
      127.0.0.1 only. The desk's URL layout over this tree and DATA:
      /desk/static/ (src/desk/), /desk/avatars/ (DATA/avatars/),
      /desk/assets/ (DATA/desk-assets/, else desk-assets/ in this tree: the
      committed base head), /tools/; POST /save/PATH writes
      DATA/PATH under avatars/, desk-assets/ or debug/. It prints a token
      for the run: pages that save are opened with #token=TOKEN and send
      it as X-Dev-Token (another page in the browser can't), and requests
      must name 127.0.0.1:PORT or localhost:PORT. Every response carries
      the desk's CSP; violations are logged to DATA/csp-reports.log.

  headless.mjs URL [--wait EXPR] [--eval EXPR] [--shot FILE]
      Headless Chrome (SwiftShader) over the DevTools protocol: opens URL,
      waits for EXPR (default window.__ready), prints the page's console,
      a value and a screenshot.

  make-base-head.mjs DATA OUT [--parts-only]
      The base head (OUT; the committed one is desk-assets/base-head.bin)
      from USC ICT's ICT-FaceKit (MIT), at a pinned commit: downloads the
      neutral head and 53 expressions into DATA/ict-facekit/ (each checked
      by SHA-256), keeps the face, the back of the head and the mouth's
      inside, simplifies them keeping every vertex where it is, maps the
      expressions onto the 52 ARKit names (base-head-lib.mjs), adds the
      teeth, gums and tongue, then runs make-base-head.html through the dev
      server in headless Chrome for the landmarks. Needs
      DATA/desk-assets/mediapipe/ (fetch-desk-assets.sh). The same inputs
      give the same file, byte for byte.

  make-base-head.html
      Its landmark step: renders ICT's neutral head, finds MediaPipe's 478
      landmarks on it and keeps them as points on its surface, the eye
      outlines moved onto the kept head's eye openings; writes
      desk-assets/base-head.bin and debug/base-render.png.

  fit-pack.html?pack=NAME#token=TOKEN
      Fits avatars/NAME's still (and closed photo) with the desk's fit.js
      and saves head.bin, eyes.png, eyemask.png and avatar.ini into it.

  fit-checks.html
      The fit's checks on real images made from avatars/butler: no face,
      two faces, eyes closed, a small face, a soft one, a tall photo, a
      closed photo moved, resized or open; the reflections removed; an
      Exif-turned copy (avatars/checks/still-exif6.jpg) fitted upright.

  avatar-preview.html
      The avatar module with buttons for each state, moment, arrive,
      speak and stop. Its query freezes a pose for screenshots: pack,
      state, shapes=jawOpen:0.3,..., pose=YAW,PITCH,ROLL, gaze=X,Y,
      breath, neutral=1 (no state's shapes), reduced=1, nogl=1, lose=1,
      bare=1 (no controls). It sets window.__ready when drawn.

  behaviour-checks.html
      The module's behaviour, live: speech from avatars/audio/voice.wav
      (0.5 s silence, 1.2 s voice, 0.4 s silence), speech replaced,
      stopped and disposed, the browser voice, frame rates, hiding, the
      states, moments, reduced motion; the drawn shut lids' lash line
      (avatars/drawn: the butler's still alone, fitted), the closed lips
      and the chin's edge as the jaw opens.

  cache-checks.html#token=TOKEN
      Against the dev server with --cache (the desk's caching: max-age
      and an ETag): a pack changed on disk is seen by the next
      createAvatar, and a head over another still of the same size shows
      the still.

  test-avatar.mjs [--write-fixture]
      node checks for fit.js's, avatar.js's and base-head-lib.mjs's pure
      parts; --write-fixture
      rewrites src/testdata/avatar/tiny-head.bin (the Zig tests' head).

Run them from harness/:

  sh tools/fetch-desk-assets.sh DATA/desk-assets
  python3 -I tools/devserver.py 8731 DATA

Keep DATA outside the repository: the butler's portraits and fitted files
aren't cleared for it (README: Avatar packs), and the ICT-FaceKit download
isn't committed (only the base head made from it).
